### Task Manager API (MongoDB) — sample requests
### Open in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension and click "Send Request".

@host = http://localhost:8082

### Home / info
GET {{host}}/

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Get all tasks
GET {{host}}/api/tasks

### Get only completed tasks
GET {{host}}/api/tasks?completed=true

### Create a task
POST {{host}}/api/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learn Spring Boot with MongoDB",
  "description": "Connect the app to MongoDB Atlas",
  "priority": "HIGH"
}

### Get one task (replace the id with a real one from the list)
GET {{host}}/api/tasks/REPLACE_WITH_ID

### Update a task
PUT {{host}}/api/tasks/REPLACE_WITH_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated title",
  "description": "Updated description",
  "completed": true,
  "priority": "MEDIUM"
}

### Toggle completion
PATCH {{host}}/api/tasks/REPLACE_WITH_ID/toggle

### Delete a task
DELETE {{host}}/api/tasks/REPLACE_WITH_ID
